<p>A system like this falls in a planning range of roughly $8,500 to $14,000 installed in Austin, depending on fixture grade and controls. It is a range, not a quote; the <a href="/tools/cost-estimator/">cost estimator</a> lets you move the levers.</p>

<h2>Austin-specific notes</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Heat.</strong> Brass and copper fixtures shrug off 105-degree afternoons; powder-coated aluminum fades and seals fail. Buy once.</li>
  <li><strong>Deer and dogs.</strong> Ground fixtures on brass stakes survive traffic; thin aluminum path lights do not.</li>
  <li><strong>Dark-sky courtesy.</strong> Shield every fixture, aim at the house or the plant and keep output modest. Your neighbors and the stars will thank you.</li>
  <li><strong>Mosquito season.</strong> Warm 2700K light attracts fewer insects than cooler white, one more reason to avoid 4000K floods.</li>
</ul>

